{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793788042,"nonce":"xg3fW7Pm3Jvthf/cb+OcxOchmm0=","title":"A Dirichlet pin on a point-set tag is refused on a multi-region domain","message":"On a domain built from named regions (`(a.name('lower') + b.name('upper')).domain()`), a pin on a `domain.tag` point set that is not a boundary region -- a single corner node, or a band of interior nodes -- classifies as a volume term on that tag and is refused with 'a residual with the trial but no test function must live on a boundary region ... Got the whole-domain volume'. The same tag works on a single-region domain. `_is_volume_region` only accepts a region with cells, so a point set never qualifies.\n\nReproduction: two named rectangles meeting at y = W/2; `dom.tag('corner', lambda x, y: (x \u003c 1e-9) \u0026 (y \u003e W - 1e-9))`; `u(*dom.variable('corner', split=True))[0] - 0.0` in the term list.\n\nWorkaround: make the pinned set a region of its own with cells (a small named rect).","files":null}]}